# agent-pr-reviewer-lite — Cursor rules

Deterministic PR risk reviewer for agent-generated code changes.
No LLM calls, no telemetry, no auth. Fully offline, filesystem + git only.

## Before starting

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` before any non-trivial change.

## Module boundaries

| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| `src/rules.ts` | Risk rules — deterministic, test-covered, pure functions |
| `src/risk.ts` | Report builder (`buildReport`, `shouldFail`) |
| `src/git.ts` | Git diff parser — no shell injection |
| `src/config.ts` | Config loading + glob-to-regex |
| `src/github.ts` | GitHub PR comment via fetch — human review required |
| `src/reporters/` | Text / JSON / Markdown output formatters |
| `src/types.ts` | All shared types and `RISK_LEVEL_ORDER` |
| `tests/` | Vitest specs — one per module minimum |

## Rule authoring

- `match(file: ChangedFile): RiskFinding[] | string | null` — no side effects
- Use `matchesAny(path, regexes)` for pattern matching
- Use the `finding(rule, file, reason)` helper for single findings
- Every new rule needs: positive match, negative match, edge case tests

## Safe git

- `git` called via `execFileSync` with argument array — never a shell string
- Null-byte validation on all ref inputs (`assertNoNullBytes`)
- Never add shell string concatenation in `src/git.ts`

## Testing

- `pnpm test` must pass before finishing any task
- `pnpm typecheck` must pass
- Isolate tests — no real git repos, no network calls
- Do not skip or disable tests

## Commit style

Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `improve:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`.
No emoji. Summary ≤ 72 chars. Body explains why.

## Forbidden without approval

- Breaking CLI flag names, exit codes, or JSON output schema
- Adding external dependencies without justification
- Changing `src/github.ts` (network path)
- Disabling tests or skipping CI
